# Copy to `.env.local` to enable Google sign-in during local development.
#
# This is a PUBLIC OAuth client id, not a secret — it ships in the JavaScript
# bundle by design. In CI it is set as a repository *variable* (not a secret)
# named VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.
#
# Leave it unset and the app runs in guest mode: everything works except
# cross-device sync.
#
# Get one at https://console.cloud.google.com:
#   1. Enable the Google Drive API
#   2. OAuth consent screen -> External -> add scope
#      https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.appdata -> add yourself as a test user
#   3. Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application
#   4. Authorised JavaScript origins must list every origin you load the app
#      from, exactly (scheme + host + port, no trailing slash):
#         http://localhost:5173          <- vite dev
#         https://<user>.github.io       <- GitHub Pages
#      Leave redirect URIs empty; this app uses the token flow, not a redirect.
#
# See README.md ("Enable Google sign-in") for the full walkthrough.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
